==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-on the table.ogg|a=AU}}

===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-prepphr}}

# {{senseid|en|up for formal discussion}} {{lb|en|politics}} Up for [[formal]] [[discussion]]; [[table]]d.
#: {{ux|en|The proposed new bill will soon be '''on the table''' in Parliament.}}
# {{senseid|en|open or available for further attention or action}} {{lb|en|idiomatic|by extension}} Open or [[available]] for further attention or action.
#: {{cot|en|on one's plate|;|in play}}
#: {{collocation|en|now everything is '''on the table'''}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=1994-06-30|author=Kenneth N. Gilpin|title=Dart Family Files Lawsuit To Nudge Brazilian Bank|url=http://www.nytimes.com/1994/06/30/business/company-news-dart-family-files-lawsuit-to-nudge-brazilian-bank.html|accessdate=2014-04-06
|passage="We made an offer about two weeks ago, which is still '''on the table'''," he said. "We have not withdrawn it, and hope they will consider it."|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160309000837/https://www.nytimes.com/1994/06/30/business/company-news-dart-family-files-lawsuit-to-nudge-brazilian-bank.html}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-04-03|author=Jonathan Broder; [[w:Matthew Cooper (American journalist)|Matthew Cooper]]|title=Iran Was the Easy Part: Obama Takes His Nuke Deal to Congress|url=http://www.newsweek.com/iran-was-easy-part-obama-takes-his-nuke-deal-congress-319336|journal=w:Newsweek|accessdate=2014-04-06
|passage=Israeli intelligence minister Yuval Steinitz said all options were open for Israel. "If we have no choice, we have no choice...the military option is '''on the table'''," he said.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260923160234/https://www.newsweek.com/iran-was-easy-part-obama-takes-his-nuke-deal-congress-319336|archivedate=23 September 2026}}
# {{&lit|en}}
#: {{ux|en|I placed the book '''on the table'''.}}

